TYPE UDT_HopperBlockageIO
  ROOTID 0
  COMMENT "Caller-visible interface (C-115) for FB_HopperBlockageMonitor. FC_ControlMain writes HopperLevelHigh/PlantRunning/FaultReset in and reads HopperBlockedAlarm/HopperBlockedInhibit out (wiring is a separate integration step). Per the Gate-1 supervisory-monitor exemption (NEW-HBA-07) this pure monitor carries no enable/ready/running vocabulary stubs. BlockedTimeThreshold/ClearDebounceTime are this instance's own tunables (C-307), commissioning defaults set as the iDB start values."
  MEMBERS
    HopperLevelHigh : Bool COMMENT "In (FC_ControlMain, from DB_Input.Hopper_Level_High at integration): hopper high-level sensor - the blockage condition this FB supervises for persistence."
    PlantRunning : Bool COMMENT "In (FC_ControlMain, from DB_Input.Shredder_Run_Fwd_FB OR Shredder_Run_Rev_FB): plant-running gate - the persistence window accrues only while the plant actually runs (Q-HBA-04), so a full hopper at standstill never alarms."
    FaultReset : Bool COMMENT "In (FC_ControlMain, from DB_Controls.FaultReset): shared operator reset - clears the latched alarm below. C-115 handshake vocabulary, verbatim across the corpus."
    BlockedTimeThreshold : Time COMMENT "Setting: cumulative high-and-running persistence threshold, seconds (start value T#60S). FB-own tunable per C-307 (not a shared DB_Settings member), commissioning-set as the iDB start value."
    ClearDebounceTime : Time COMMENT "Setting: confirmed-clear filter time, seconds (start value T#2S) - the hopper must read clear continuously this long before the window re-arms, rejecting sensor chatter (Q-HBA-02). FB-own tunable per C-307, commissioning-set."
    HopperBlockedAlarm : Bool COMMENT "Out: latched hopper-blockage alarm (REQ-HBA-001/004). RETAIN - deliberately survives a power cycle (C-124 carve-out), cleared only by FaultReset, like the sequencer's DischargeConveyorTimeoutFault; a blockage needing a human still needs acknowledgement after a restart."
    HopperBlockedInhibit : Bool COMMENT "Out: stop/inhibit demand (Q-HBA-05) - tracks the latched alarm and, being RETAIN, correspondingly persists across a power cycle until acknowledged. The FB writes no shared tag; integration wires this demand to the actual stop separately."
